# Roast Commands

Evidence-based code review. Not comedy. Every finding cites `path:line`, diff, or test output. Output in chat only — no roast markdown files in the repo.

**Before any roast:** run `npx roast context` and `npx roast diff --base auto` (or read equivalent INIT data). Load the `roast` skill.

## Commands

| Command | Mode | Behavior |
|---------|------|----------|
| `/roast` | roast-and-fix | INIT → findings → minimal fix → verify |
| `/roast-only` | roast-only | INIT → findings → verdict — **no file edits** |
| `/roast-idea` | roast-idea | Critique proposal/plan before any implementation |
| `/roast-ui` | roast-only (frontend) | Scope: components, styles, a11y, client state |
| `/roast-api` | roast-only (backend) | Scope: handlers, schema, auth, errors, API contracts |

## Natural language triggers

Same modes via chat:
- "roast independently" → roast-only
- "roast and fix" → roast-and-fix
- "roast this idea before implementing" → roast-idea
- "don't patch" / "senior architect" → roast-no-patch

## Output shape

```markdown
## 🔥 Roast: [target]
### Context (init) ...
### The real problem ...
### Findings (🔴🟠🟡🟢 with path:line) ...
### Fix path ... (fix modes only)
```

## Hard rules

- NEVER roast without Phase 0 INIT
- NEVER vague findings
- NEVER write unsolicited `*_ROAST.md` files
- NEVER edit files in `/roast-only`, `/roast-ui`, `/roast-api`, `/roast-idea` unless user escalates
